The provided excerpt does not report quantitative experimental outcomes, numerical comparisons, or statistical significance for WERM-ID-R, WERM-ID, or the plug-in estimator. It only states qualitatively that the heuristic procedure of learning the weight and prediction function separately works well in practice.
[context]
Experiments use synthetic data generated from specified structural causal models for three causal graphs. Ground truth for the intervened outcome is computed by drawing 10 million samples from the intervened structural model. The hypothesis and weight classes are gradient boosting regression models. The excerpt reports a time complexity of O(m log m) for the gradient boosting-based estimation and optimization steps, but does not provide dataset sample sizes, hardware, hyperparameters, loss values, or evaluation metrics beyond the described comparison.
