In synthetic system identification with hidden dimensions N in {4, 6, 7, 8, 16}, the restricted-capacity uRNN achieved comparable or better test mean-squared error than the full-capacity uRNN for N < 7, the two models were relatively comparable at N = 7 with the full-capacity uRNN achieving slightly lower error, and the full-capacity uRNN always achieved better test mean-squared error for N > 7. The provided excerpt does not report the numerical mean-squared error values, confidence intervals, or statistical significance. In the speech frame prediction task, the paper reports comparisons among full-capacity uRNN, restricted-capacity uRNN, and LSTM in a table and example predictions, but the provided text does not include the numerical loss values or significance tests.
