The provided excerpt does not report numeric FID or Inception score values. It reports that the baseline with spectral normalization only in the discriminator and 1:1 updates became very unstable and exhibited early mode collapse, with examples shown at the 10k-th iteration. Adding spectral normalization to both generator and discriminator stabilized training under 1:1 updates, but sample quality as measured by FID and Inception score began to drop around the 260k-th iteration. Adding imbalanced learning rates produced monotonic improvement in sample quality and no significant decrease in FID or Inception score over one million training iterations, supporting an additive effect of the two stabilization techniques.
