osed uniform perturbation δx ~ U(-0.1, 0.1)^dim(x) is not validated by the related work: [(Shen et al., 2021-02)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/33accfad821a4aee5ef96fb2ee48e1c2a774401a) shows perturbation severity must be aligned across factors using FID and that different channels produce different errors at similar FID, implying a fixed coordinate-wise uniform scale may be too crude for high-dimensional or multimodal covariates such as UTK-sim and TC-sim. Sixth, sample-size and distributional concerns arise: [(Zhou et al., 2021-10)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/704203c476d4be7aa650f5799d7f69b2569b2e0c) shows Gaussian-assumption methods are stable in small samples but can be limited by distribution mismatch, and GANITE needs more than 15,000 samples for competitive results, which contradicts the feasibility of strong conclusions from UTK-sim with only 1,000 units unless convergence and multiple outcome realizations are reported. Finally, [(Kuzmanovic et al., 2022-03)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/ebd6491c702866ce55887cacd5dd57bb78b2e079) provides no quantitative outcomes in the excerpt and targets missing treatment rather than covariate perturbation, so it cannot substantiate the plan's robust CATE claims.",
  "suggested_action": "The most important action is to add a direct perturbation benchmark that reports sqrtPEHE, PEHE, ATE/ATT error, and policy risk under no perturbation, uniform, FGSM, and OTCM for all baselines, with confidence intervals or bootstrap standard errors, because the cited HTE works use PEHE/ATE/policy risk but do not provide robustness evidence; align the IHDP protocol with [(Shalit et al., 2016-06)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/17409ae85c237983dc22a5e4750d8054e4b6edc9) by specifying 747 units, 25 covariates, outcome realizations, 63/27/10 splits, and treatment imbalance, and align ACIC with the exact 4,802/82 version used in the plan rather than the 5,000/177 version in [(Chikahara, and Ushiyama, 2024-04)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/679a8718d4b5fa0eeb57052aafa620aaf2b9df8a). Second, tune α, β, IPM weight, Lipschitz penalty, learning rate, batch size, and architecture width on validation data instead of fixing α=β=1, batch 64, learning rate 0.01, and 200/100 units, using the hyperparameter sensitivity evidence from [(Johansson et al., 2016-05)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/759b00cf35b397eab468935b5d90d04e9ed25549) and the validation-tuned high-dimensional setup in [(Chikahara, and Ushiyama, 2024-04)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/679a8718d4b5fa0eeb57052aafa620aaf2b9df8a); include ablations that separate IPM, Lipschitz orthonormality, and RKHS terms. Third, for UTK-sim and TC-sim, define perturbation severity in a data-aware way rather than only coordinate-wise uniform noise, inspired by [(Shen et al., 2021-02)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/33accfad821a4aee5ef96fb2ee48e1c2a774401a), e.g., normalize features, use FID or distributional distance to align perturbation levels, and test channel/text-block-specific perturbations because high-dimensional covariates may have heterogeneous sensitivity. Fourth, report sample-size convergence and multiple outcome realizations for UTK-sim with 1,000 units and for syn